  "hints": [
    "this is 'two sum' but with an extra fixed element - could sorting help you avoid the third nested loop?",
    "once the array is sorted, for a fixed first element, can you find the other two with pointers moving toward each other instead of a nested loop?",
    "for a fixed i, use left = i+1 and right = end; move left up if the sum is too small, right down if too large",
    "after finding a valid triplet, how do you skip past duplicate values for i, left, and right so you don't add the same triplet twice?"
  ],
  "commonMistakes": [
    "not skipping duplicate values, producing repeated triplets in the output",
    "not sorting first, which breaks the two-pointer approach entirely",
    "using nested loops for the inner search anyway, missing the point of two pointers"
  ],
  "content": {
